    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 93,
      "bottomRightX": 678,
      "bottomRightY": 131,
      "content": "We assume that the potential $U$ can be developed in powers of $r^{-1}$; for a neutral atom, one will then have the dipole terms:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 327,
      "topLeftY": 135,
      "bottomRightX": 677,
      "bottomRightY": 169,
      "content": "$$U(x, y, z) = \\frac{e}{r^3} (\\mathfrak{P}\\mathfrak{r}) \\tag{1}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 189,
      "bottomRightX": 678,
      "bottomRightY": 232,
      "content": "in the first approximation, where $\\mathfrak{P}(q)$ is the electric moment of the atom. We then associate it with the matrix $\\mathfrak{P}_{nm}$. From (6), § 7, one will then have:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 327,
      "topLeftY": 254,
      "bottomRightX": 677,
      "bottomRightY": 296,
      "content": "$$V_{nm} = \\frac{8\\pi^2 \\mu e}{h^2} \\left( \\mathfrak{P}_{nm} \\frac{\\mathfrak{r}}{r^3} \\right). \\tag{2}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 316,
      "bottomRightX": 678,
      "bottomRightY": 370,
      "content": "Naturally, this Ansatz can only be correct for electrons that pass by the atom at the distance considered. We therefore restrict our consideration to electrons for which $r > r_0$ ($^1$), and thus write, from (13), § 6:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 190,
      "topLeftY": 388,
      "bottomRightX": 601,
      "bottomRightY": 430,
      "content": "$$f_0^\\infty(-k_{nm}\\mathfrak{s}) = \\frac{1}{4\\pi^2 i k_{nm}} \\int_{r_0}^\\infty \\rho \\, d\\rho \\left\\{ F_{nm}(\\rho\\mathfrak{s}) e^{-i\\rho k_{nm}} - F_{nm}(-\\rho\\mathfrak{s}) e^{i\\rho k_{nm}} \\right\\}.$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 450,
      "bottomRightX": 678,
      "bottomRightY": 485,
      "content": "We now assume that that the incoming electrons define a parallel bundle, which corresponds to a plane wave; one will then have:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 254,
      "topLeftY": 504,
      "bottomRightX": 535,
      "bottomRightY": 548,
      "content": "$$F_{nm}(r\\mathfrak{s}) = V_{nm} e^{ik\\rho\\mathfrak{s}_z} = \\frac{8\\pi^2 \\mu e}{h^2} (\\mathfrak{P}_{nm}, \\mathfrak{s}) \\frac{e^{ik\\rho\\mathfrak{s}_z}}{\\rho^2}.$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 565,
      "bottomRightX": 276,
      "bottomRightY": 583,
      "content": "Moreover, one will have:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 279,
      "topLeftY": 587,
      "bottomRightX": 677,
      "bottomRightY": 623,
      "content": "$$i \\pi k_{nm} f_0^\\infty(-k_{nm}\\mathfrak{s}) = 4\\pi \\frac{\\mu e}{h^2} (\\mathfrak{P}_{nm}, \\mathfrak{s}) A, \\tag{3}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 642,
      "bottomRightX": 375,
      "bottomRightY": 660,
      "content": "for which, with $\\mathfrak{s}_z = \\cos \\vartheta$, one will have:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 279,
      "topLeftY": 683,
      "bottomRightX": 677,
      "bottomRightY": 725,
      "content": "$$A = \\int_{r_0}^\\infty \\frac{d\\rho}{\\rho} \\cos [r (k \\cos \\vartheta - k_{nm})], \\tag{4}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 728,
      "bottomRightX": 132,
      "bottomRightY": 740,
      "content": "or",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 279,
      "topLeftY": 743,
      "bottomRightX": 677,
      "bottomRightY": 764,
      "content": "$$A = - C_i (r_0 [k \\cos \\vartheta - k_{nm}]), \\tag{5}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 778,
